       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. It is also well above the 2,000 mg maximum for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled range:\n- **Metformin IR 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Metformin IR 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Metformin IR 1,700 mg total per day, divided.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, or if you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. I'll also need to know whether you want IR or XR."
      }
